From 73d61911235a2cde09d2ec64edf884697fe5c404 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:33:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] arm64: dts: qcom: a70q: enable CPU power collapse

The A70 downstream power description uses PSCI CPU mode 0x3 with the same per-cluster latency values already present in Talos.

Enable only this shallow leaf state. Leave rail power collapse and every shared cluster state disabled so firmware acceptance and wake reliability can be validated independently.

Signed-off-by: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts | 11 ++---------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts
index dd622fe2f..57624acd4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6150-samsung-a70q.dts
@@ -276,20 +276,13 @@ &venus_opp_table {
 
 /*
  * Match the cluster modes and latency ordering used by the A70 firmware.
- * Keep every non-WFI state disabled until it passes staged validation.
+ * Enable CPU power collapse first; keep rail and cluster collapse disabled
+ * until the shallower state passes staged validation.
  */
-&little_cpu_sleep_0 {
-	status = "disabled";
-};
-
 &little_cpu_sleep_1 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
-&big_cpu_sleep_0 {
-	status = "disabled";
-};
-
 &big_cpu_sleep_1 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
